mentModifierV","text":"AccessibilityAttachmentModifier","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"extendedModule":"SwiftUICore"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"references":{"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami":{"abstract":[{"text":"An Origami → SwiftUI translator: a deterministic parser reads Facebook’s ","type":"text"},{"code":".origami","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"patch graph into a semantic IR, and a codegen writes that IR out as SwiftUI. Swami","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is also the patch-matched helper library that fills gaps between Origami patches","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and native SwiftUI — one helper per Origami patch, named after the patch, sized by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Origami’s patch surface. Every pattern that lands is a deliverable, verified against","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Origami’s own render, and shipped as a DocC-embedded example.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swami","role":"collection","title":"Swami"},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami/Interaction_PinchView/accessibilityDragPoint(_:description:isEnabled:)-4f7g2":{"abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/swami\/interaction_pinchview\/accessibilitydragpoint(_:description:isenabled:)-4f7g2","role":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"accessibilityDragPoint(_:description:isEnabled:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction_PinchView\/accessibilityDragPoint(_:description:isEnabled:)-4f7g2","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"accessibilityDragPoint","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"S","kind":"genericParameter"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"UnitPoint","preciseIdentifier":"s:7SwiftU